<section id="expertise" aria-label="Expertise" class="sec-3d">
  <canvas id="exp-3d" aria-hidden="true" class="sec-canvas"></canvas>
  <div class="sec-bg-orb sec-orb-1" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="wrap" style="position: relative; z-index: 1;">
    <div class="sec-tag reveal">What I Do</div>
    <h2 class="sec-h2 reveal d1">Four disciplines. One integrated system.</h2>
    <p class="sec-lead reveal d2">SEO, AI search visibility, content strategy, and marketing automation. Most teams hire separately for each. I run them as one compounding system where every discipline accelerates the others.</p>
    <div class="exp-grid exp-grid-4">
      <div class="exp-card reveal"><div class="exp-icon ei-indigo"><span class="exp-num">01</span></div><h3>SEO Management</h3><p>Full-program SEO ownership: technical audits, site architecture, crawl optimization, Core Web Vitals, schema markup, and indexation governance. I build the compounding foundations competitors take months to catch up to.</p></div>
      <div class="exp-card reveal d1"><div class="exp-icon ei-violet"><span class="exp-num">02</span></div><h3>AI Search Visibility</h3><p>GEO and AEO for brands that need to be cited, not just ranked. Entity frameworks, retrieval-ready content, and structured signals that put your brand inside ChatGPT, Gemini, Claude, and Google AI Overviews before your competitors appear.</p></div>
      <div class="exp-card reveal d2"><div class="exp-icon ei-amber"><span class="exp-num">03</span></div><h3>Content Strategy</h3><p>Topic cluster architecture, search intent modeling, and editorial frameworks built for how AI models interpret authority. Content that ranks today and earns citations tomorrow, without needing a full production team to maintain it.</p></div>
      <div class="exp-card reveal d3"><div class="exp-icon ei-cyan"><span class="exp-num">04</span></div><h3>Marketing Automation</h3><p>LLM and n8n workflows that eliminate manual reporting, content production overhead, and repetitive SEO tasks. Auditable systems with measurable output quality, built so teams scale execution without scaling headcount.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ══════════════ FEATURED WORK TEASER ══════════════ -->
<section id="work" class="cases-sec sec-3d" aria-label="Selected Work" style="background: var(--bg-1);">
  <canvas id="cases-3d" aria-hidden="true" class="sec-canvas"></canvas>
  <div class="sec-bg-orb sec-orb-2" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="wrap" style="position: relative; z-index: 1;">
    <div class="sec-tag reveal">Selected Work</div>
    <h2 class="sec-h2 reveal d1">The work, not the pitch</h2>
    <p class="sec-lead reveal d2">Five projects across AEO/LLM visibility, SEO management, content strategy, and product launches — each with a clear problem, a clear approach, and numbers that hold up. Here's the headline one.</p>
    <div class="cases-grid">
      <div class="case-card featured reveal">
        <div class="case-card-top-bar bar-green"></div>
        <div class="case-pill pill-green">AEO / LLM Visibility · Featured</div>
        <div class="case-meta">Wellows · July 2025 – Feb 2026 · Source: GA4 / Looker Studio / GSC</div>
        <div class="case-nums">
          <div><div class="cn-val green">9×</div><div class="cn-lbl">LLM Growth</div></div>
          <div><div class="cn-val green">62.9→27.8</div><div class="cn-lbl">Avg. SERP Position</div></div>
          <div><div class="cn-val green">45s→6+ min</div><div class="cn-lbl">Session Duration</div></div>
          <div><div class="cn-val green">~1.9M</div><div class="cn-lbl">GSC Impressions</div></div>
          <div><div class="cn-val green">$0</div><div class="cn-lbl">Paid Spend</div></div>
        </div>
        <h3>9× LLM Growth and #1–#2 Tool Rankings — Built Entirely on AEO, $0 Paid</h3>
        <p>Wellows started with near-zero LLM visibility and no citation footprint. I built measurable AI-search presence from scratch — zero paid spend.</p>
        <ul class="case-approach">
          <li><b>AEO framework.</b> Koray Tuğberk's logic + Google's query fan-out patent for LLM retrieval.</li>
          <li><b>Citation experiments.</b> Grounded vs. non-grounded tests tracking explicit and implicit AI visibility.</li>
          <li><b>Tool- &amp; community-led.</b> Three AI tools as LLM entry points; AEO across Reddit, Quora, G2; n8n + GA4 reporting.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="case-growth">
          <div class="case-growth-label">Traffic Growth · GSC-verified</div>
          <div class="case-growth-grid">
            <figure class="case-shot">
              <a href="/static/uploads/gsctrafficgrowth.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="/static/uploads/gsctrafficgrowth.png" alt="Google Search Console: 7.27K clicks and 3.78M impressions over the last 3 months, average position improving from 28.9 to 17.3" loading="lazy"></a>
              <figcaption>7.27K clicks · 3.78M impressions · avg. position 28.9 → 17.3 (last 3 months vs. previous)</figcaption>
            </figure>
            <figure class="case-shot">
              <a href="/static/uploads/gscyearoveryear.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="/static/uploads/gscyearoveryear.jpg" alt="Google Search Console year over year: clicks 10.7K to 23.6K and impressions 275K to 928K, 2025 vs 2024" loading="lazy"></a>
              <figcaption>Year over year: 10.7K → 23.6K clicks · 275K → 928K impressions (2025 vs. 2024)</figcaption>
            </figure>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="work-teaser-foot reveal d1">
      <a href="/work/" class="btn-primary">See all five case studies →</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ══════════════ TOOLS TEASER ══════════════ -->
<section id="tools" class="sec-3d" aria-label="Proprietary Tools">
  <canvas id="tools-3d" aria-hidden="true" class="sec-canvas"></canvas>
  <div class="sec-bg-orb sec-orb-3" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="wrap" style="position: relative; z-index: 1;">
    <div class="sec-tag reveal">Proprietary Tools</div>
    <h2 class="sec-h2 reveal d1" style="max-width:620px">Tools I built to bridge search science and AI retrieval</h2>
    <p class="sec-lead reveal d2">Three instruments grounded in Google patent research, used by 1,647 practitioners worldwide, acquired entirely through organic search.</p>
    <div class="tools-grid">
      <div class="tool-card reveal"><div class="tool-badge">829 Active Users</div><h3>Query Fan-Out Generator</h3><p>Built on Google's Query Fan-Out patent research, it generates the full semantic expansion of any seed query so your content covers how search engines and LLMs interpret intent — not just exact-match keywords.</p><a href="/tools/" class="tool-link">Explore the tools →</a></div>
      <div class="tool-card reveal d1"><div class="tool-badge">AI Search · 149 Users</div><h3>LLM Query Builder</h3><p>Constructs optimized query structures for LLM-based SEO research and entity mapping. Built for practitioners who need to work with AI retrieval systematically, not ad hoc.</p><a href="/tools/" class="tool-link">Explore the tools →</a></div>
      <div class="tool-card reveal d2"><div class="tool-badge">669 Users · 60–72% Engagement</div><h3>AI Humanizer</h3><p>Transforms AI-generated drafts into content that reads naturally, holds topical depth, and aligns with how LLMs evaluate quality signals. Users work with it, not through it.</p><a href="/tools/" class="tool-link">Explore the tools →</a></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

